session Continuous_Path_Spaces = Continuous_Time_Martingales +
  description "
    Weak convergence of processes done properly: C([0,T],'b) as a Polish
    space with portmanteau and the continuous mapping theorem, tightness of a
    family of path laws from increment moments alone, and quadratic variation
    as an adapted, everywhere-continuous path functional with a summable L2
    rate -- and the exit time of a closed set by a continuous path, upper
    semicontinuous along weak convergence of path laws.
  "
  options [document = pdf, document_output = "output"]
  sessions
    Kolmogorov_Chentsov
    Levy_Prokhorov_Metric
    Standard_Borel_Spaces
    Semicontinuous_Analysis
    "HOL-Complex_Analysis"
  theories
    Increment_Moments
    Increment_Tails
    Dyadic_Chaining
    Modulus_Tails
    Holder_Interpolation
    Conditional_UI
    Equicontinuity
    Path_Space
    Path_Exit_Times
    Path_Tightness
    Path_Space_Infinite
    Stopped_Localization
    Pathwise_Quadratic_Variation
    Adapted_Quadratic_Variation
  document_files
    "root.tex"
    "root.bib"
